# weddle's pull-only mirror of every account, run by
# systemd/user/mail-pull.service as `mbsync -c ~/.dotfiles/mail/mbsyncrc-weddle -a`.
# Sync Pull with Near-only Create/Remove/Expunge never writes to the server,
# so it can't race daysy, the one full client (README.md).
#
# Paths are absolute under /data/Maildir-imap rather than via ~/Maildir, so
# repointing that symlink can never aim mbsync at a tree another host writes
# into. No MaxSize: in mbsyncrc it stops doomed uploads, but here it would
# skip large downloads without a word.

IMAPAccount personal
Host imap.fastmail.com
Port 993
AuthMech PLAIN
User benswift@fastmail.com
PassCmd "$HOME/.dotfiles/bin/mail-secret get benswift@fastmail.com mbsync-fastmail"
TLSType IMAPS
PipelineDepth 50

IMAPStore personal-remote
Account personal

MaildirStore personal-local
Path /data/Maildir-imap/personal/
Inbox /data/Maildir-imap/personal/INBOX
SubFolders Verbatim

Channel personal
Far :personal-remote:
Near :personal-local:
Patterns INBOX Archive "Sent Items" Drafts Trash "Junk Mail" DMARC
Create Near
Remove Near
Sync Pull
Expunge Near
SyncState *
CopyArrivalDate yes

